// =============================================================================
// 01-discover-search-diagnostic-shape.kql
// RUN THIS SECOND. Files 10, 11, 12, and 22 all depend on its answer.
// =============================================================================
//
// PURPOSE
//   Confirm which AzureDiagnostics columns the Azure AI Search service actually
//   populates in this workspace, and settle empirically whether Search ever
//   emits 206 into resultSignature_d.
//
// WHY THIS QUERY EXISTS (open item U6)
//   Azure AI Search has NO dedicated Log Analytics table. Its resource logs land
//   in the shared AzureDiagnostics table alongside every other provider, which
//   is why every Search query in this library filters on
//   ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.SEARCH".
//   The documented Properties sub-schema is only Description_s, Documents_d,
//   IndexName_s, and Query_s. The KQL column names carry type suffixes and
//   differ from the logical names in the data reference: write resultSignature_d
//   (lowercase r, _d suffix), not ResultSignature, and DurationMs, not
//   DurationMS.
//   Separately, no Microsoft sample confirms that 206 Partial Content ever
//   reaches resultSignature_d. Half the Search-side 206 tooling depends on that
//   being true. Section 3 of this query settles it with data.
//   Research: .copilot-tracking/research/2026-09-22/ai-search-scaling-206-403-rca-research.md
//             Lines 188-200 (D11 schema limitation), Lines 425-440 (U6)
//
// TARGET TABLE
//   AzureDiagnostics, filtered to ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.SEARCH".
//
// PREREQUISITES
//   * A diagnostic setting on the Search service sending OperationLogs (and
//     ideally AllMetrics) to this Log Analytics workspace.
//   Enable with: scripts/Enable-DiagnosticSettings.ps1
//
// HEALTHY VS UNHEALTHY
//   Healthy   : section 1 lists resultSignature_d, DurationMs, IndexName_s,
//               Documents_d, OperationName; section 2 shows all seven indexes;
//               section 3 shows overwhelmingly 200.
//   Unhealthy : section 3 shows non-trivial counts of 403, 429, or 503.
//   Notable   : section 3 shows 206. That CONFIRMS U6 and makes file 11's
//               206 bucket real rather than speculative. If 206 is absent,
//               Search-side 206 detection is not viable in this workspace and
//               file 21 (APIM response-body capture) becomes the only route.
//   Blocked   : zero rows. The diagnostic setting is missing or points at a
//               different workspace.
//
// Derived from Q0-DiscoverSearchLogSchema / Q0b-DoesSearchEmit206,
//   .copilot-tracking/research/subagents/2026-09-22/observability-workbooks-kql-research.md Lines 386-412
// =============================================================================

let lookback = 7d;
// --- SECTION 1: which columns are actually populated -------------------------
AzureDiagnostics
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| where ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.SEARCH"
| getschema
| project ColumnName, ColumnType
| order by ColumnName asc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SECTION 2: which operations and which indexes are live
// Confirms the seven-index fan-out is visible in the logs and shows the exact
// IndexName_s spellings to reuse in files 10, 11, and 22.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let lookback = 7d;
// AzureDiagnostics
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
// | where ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.SEARCH"
// | summarize
//     Operations   = count(),
//     Indexes      = make_set(IndexName_s, 25),
//     DistinctIdx  = dcount(IndexName_s),
//     FirstSeen    = min(TimeGenerated),
//     LastSeen     = max(TimeGenerated)
//     by OperationName
// | order by Operations desc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SECTION 3: does Search emit 206? (the U6 decision point)
// Run this one on its own and read the StatusCode column carefully.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let lookback = 7d;
// AzureDiagnostics
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
// | where ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.SEARCH"
// | extend StatusCode = toint(resultSignature_d)
// | summarize
//     Count     = count(),
//     Indexes   = make_set(IndexName_s, 25),
//     FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated),
//     LastSeen  = max(TimeGenerated)
//     by StatusCode, OperationName, ResultType
// | order by Count desc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SECTION 4: is Query_s populated?
// Query_s is documented but never exercised in a published Microsoft sample.
// It carries the literal query string, which is the only way to tell a semantic
// query apart from a plain one in the logs. File 12 depends on it.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let lookback = 1d;
// AzureDiagnostics
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
// | where ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.SEARCH"
// | where OperationName == "Query.Search"
// | project TimeGenerated, IndexName_s, Query_s, Description_s, Documents_d, DurationMs, resultSignature_d
// | take 25
